{"result":"{
  "id": "17831",
  "key": "SFCC-5",
  "summary": "Product Detail Page (PDP)",
  "description": "**Epic Name:** Product Detail Page (PDP)\n\n**Epic Summary**\n\nThis epic covers the build of the Product Detail Page in the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. It includes the imagery gallery, size and colour selection, real-time inventory display, add-to-bag and wishlist actions, product content from Contentful/Vimeo, and supporting features such as size guides, Notify Me, and Find in Boutique. It depends on the product data model configured in the Product Catalogue epic (SFCC-4).\n\n**Business Value / Objective**\n\nThe PDP is the primary conversion point for Zimmermann's customers. A well-built PDP that accurately surfaces product information, availability, and imagery directly supports purchase confidence and reduces drop-off. It must reflect Zimmermann's premium brand experience across all 8 regional storefronts.\n\n**Scope**\n\nIn Scope:\n\n- Product imagery gallery (multi-image, zoom, colour variant switching)\n- Size and colour selection with real-time per-size inventory display\n- Out-of-stock size indication and Notify Me (back-in-stock) trigger\n- Add-to-bag and add-to-wishlist actions\n- Size guide display logic\n- Product content rendering (description, attributes sourced from SFCC/AP21)\n- Vimeo video embed support\n- Find in Boutique modal (per-boutique availability, Google Maps, geolocation)\n- Buffer stock display logic (buffered inventory feed applied on PDP)\n- Product badges display (e.g. New, Sale, Runway)\n\nOut of Scope:\n\n- Product attribute and data model configuration — covered in SFCC-4 (Product Catalogue)\n- Sorting and filtering — covered in PLP / Search epics SFCC-6, SFCC-7\n- Inventory list setup and reservation logic — covered in SFCC-11 (Cart)\n- Pricing display logic and pricebook setup — covered in SFCC-18 (Pricing)\n- Content authoring in Contentful \n- MuleSoft / AP21 feed development \n\n**Dependencies**\n\n- MuleSoft/AP21 product feed — product data must be flowing into SFCC before PDP can be tested end-to-end\n- Contentful cartridge integration — for product content and video URL references\n- Figma designs from design team\n- Open decision: Vimeo vs Contentful video hosting approach — must be resolved before PDP component build begins\n\n**Assumptions & Constraints**\n\n- AP21 is the source of truth for product data; SFCC renders what it receives via MuleSoft\n- Two inventory feeds are in scope: a buffered feed for PDP stock display and a true physical inventory feed for Find in Boutique\n- Notify Me subscriptions are stored in SFCC; the notification trigger mechanism (likely Emarsys) is to be confirmed\n- Regional content variations are managed via Contentful's locale model",
  "status": {
    "name": "In Progress",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Epic"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "High"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Squad-A"
  ]
}"}

